---
/**
 * /visibility/ — the sixth published figure, 2026-09-11.
 *
 * D93'S STANDING WARNING SAID TO REFUSE A SIXTH FIGURE UNLESS IT IS AS OBVIOUSLY
 * SEPARATE AS THE FIFTH. The test was run and the argument is written beside
 * VISIBILITY_MONTHLY_USD in src/lib/pricing.js. Read it before changing a number
 * here, and do not add a seventh figure to this page.
 *
 * THE OPERATOR OVERRODE A RECOMMENDATION TO BUILD THIS, with the cost stated
 * first: that the plan proposing it said to gather three months of real data before
 * charging anybody. He chose to publish now, so THIS PAGE DESCRIBES A METHOD AND A
 * REFUSAL AND NEVER A RESULT. Not one sentence says what has been found, because
 * nothing has been found yet. A later pass adding "clients typically see…" would
 * look like completing the page and would destroy the only thing being sold.
 *
 * THE METHOD IS PUBLISHED BECAUSE THAT IS THE WHOLE DIFFERENTIATOR. Two firms in
 * these counties already claim this category and neither publishes one. Anybody can
 * ask an assistant a question; what nobody in the sweep would do is say out loud
 * that they cannot show their work caused an answer to change.
 *
 * THE REFUSAL LIVES IN THE ENGINE, NOT HERE. src/lib/assistant-visibility.js
 * exports CAUSATION_REFUSAL and returns a named refusal in `problems` for every
 * shape it cannot report on, so no surface can print the figures without the
 * sentence. This page renders that export rather than restating it — a second copy
 * in a sales voice drifts the moment one is softened in a copy pass, which is the
 * defect D97 exists to prevent across the three comparison sheets.
 *
 * THE ENGINE REACHES NOTHING AND MUST NOT LEARN TO. The plan's stop condition was
 * aimed at the wrong rule: REACHABLE_HOSTS governs automated claim probes, not a
 * product's runtime, and this product's runtime is a person asking questions. D49
 * and L-248 mean a client's own website is never fetched to see whether an
 * assistant cited it, permanently.
 *
 * NO PAY BUTTON, for the reason /advisory/ and /ai-fit/ have none: the question set
 * has to be agreed before a first reading exists, so this starts in a conversation.
 */
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import { visibility } from '../data/services';
import { CAUSATION_REFUSAL } from '../lib/assistant-visibility.js';
import { Search, ShieldOff, ArrowUpRight } from '@lucide/astro';

const origin = new URL(Astro.site!).origin;

const schema = [
  {
    '@type': 'Service',
    '@id': `${origin}/visibility/#service`,
    name: 'AI assistant visibility measurement',
    serviceType: 'Measurement and reporting',
    provider: { '@id': `${origin}/#business` },
    description:
      'A monthly reading of whether AI assistants name your business, with the questions published and no claim about what caused a change.',
  },
];
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="Does an assistant name you?"
  description={`A monthly reading of whether AI assistants name your business, with the questions published and no claim about what caused a change. ${visibility.amount} a month.`}
  schema={schema}
>
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden border-b border-line">
    <div class="bg-grid bg-grid-fade pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 -z-10 opacity-60"></div>
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 pt-16 pb-10 sm:pt-24 sm:pb-14">
      <p class="mono-label">Measured monthly · questions published · no minimum</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 max-w-3xl font-display text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-5xl">
        Does an assistant name you?
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        {visibility.whoItIsFor}
      </p>

      <div class="mt-8 max-w-2xl">
        <div class="panel flex flex-col gap-2 p-6">
          <p class="font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink">{visibility.line}</p>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">{visibility.qualifier}</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      {/* THE REFUSAL RENDERS BESIDE THE FIGURE AND COMES FROM THE ENGINE. Below
          the fold it reads as a disclaimer; here it reads as the terms, and it is
          the actual reason this costs anything rather than being a free opinion. */}
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">{CAUSATION_REFUSAL}</p>

      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
        <a class="btn-primary" href="/contact/?intent=consult">
          Ask what you would be measured on <ArrowUpRight class="size-4" />
        </a>
        <a class="link-sweep text-sm" href="/check/">Or try the free check first →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ── The method, published ──────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
  <section class="section-band">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-16 sm:py-20">
      <p class="flex items-center gap-2.5">
        <span class="section-index">/ 01</span>
        <span class="mono-label">How it is measured</span>
      </p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 max-w-2xl font-display text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">
        The method, in full, before you buy it.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        Two firms near here sell something like this and neither says how they do it. Here is how,
        and you can check every step of it against the report you get.
      </p>

      <ol class="mt-8 grid max-w-3xl gap-3">
        {visibility.method.map((step, i) => (
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            <span class="mono-label mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-cyan-deep">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <span>{step}</span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>

      <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-faint">{visibility.firstMonth}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ── What it refuses to do ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-14 sm:py-20">
    <p class="flex items-center gap-2.5">
      <span class="section-index">/ 02</span>
      <span class="mono-label">What it will not tell you</span>
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-3 max-w-2xl font-display text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">
      The part nobody else writes down.
    </h2>

    <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
      {visibility.refuses.map((r) => (
        <div class="panel flex items-start gap-3 p-6">
          <ShieldOff class="mt-0.5 size-5 shrink-0 text-accent" aria-hidden="true" />
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">{r}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="panel mt-8 flex flex-col gap-3 p-7">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
        <Search class="size-5 text-secondary" />
        <span class="mono-label">Why that is worth paying for</span>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        A report that claimed credit would be worth more to me and less to you. Every month this
        tells you what moved and hands you the questions, so you can judge it yourself rather than
        take my word for it — and if nothing is moving, you find that out from me rather than after
        a year of invoices.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</MarketingLayout>
